<BaseLayout lang="en" title="About | Research AI Commons" description="The purpose and principles of Research AI Commons.">
<section class="section"><div class="container prose"><div class="eyebrow">About</div><h1 style="font-size:clamp(2.5rem,6vw,4.7rem)">Start with research,<br/>not the AI.</h1><p class="lead">Generative AI is entering many parts of research, yet real practices, verification methods, failures, and risks often remain inside individual labs. Research AI Commons is a place to exchange that practical knowledge across labs and disciplines.</p><h2>Core principles</h2><h3>Research comes first</h3><p>Our goal is not to maximize AI adoption. We begin with what researchers are trying to achieve and ask where AI genuinely helps—or does not.</p><h3>Share practice, not just knowledge</h3><p>We value real workflows over general advice. Failures are as welcome as successes.</p><h3>Across labs, across disciplines</h3><p>Starting from experimental research, we seek exchange with computational fields, clinical research, the humanities, social sciences, and other research cultures.</p><h3>Open, but responsible</h3><p>We respect unpublished data, collaborations, intellectual property, personal information, and institutional policies. Public insights are anonymized when needed.</p><h3>Tool-neutral</h3><p>We do not promote any particular AI product or company. We want to discuss the strengths and weaknesses of every tool openly.</p></div></section>
</BaseLayout>
